ClaudeReader - A comics and manga reader

Based on BDReader, Vincent Crocher 2014-2016 (http://bdreader.sourceforge.net/), GPLv3 or later.

Features: automatic panel detection (read a page panel by panel), strip and
page modes, manga mode (right to left), comics library with thumbnails,
resume where you left off, and a store to search and download comics and manga
(MangaDex, Mangapill, Nyaa, and your own Lua store scripts). Opens PDF, EPUB, XPS, FB2, MOBI, CBZ, CBR, CB7, CBT,
ZIP, RAR, 7Z, TAR and image folders.

Building
--------
Dependencies: a C++17 compiler, CMake >= 3.20, FLTK 1.4, OpenCV (core, imgproc,
imgcodecs; geometry for OpenCV 5), MuPDF, libarchive, libcurl, gumbo and Lua 5.4+
(static library).

Windows (MSYS2, https://www.msys2.org):
    pacman -S mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-toolchain mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-cmake \
              mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-ninja mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-pkgconf \
              mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-fltk mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-opencv \
              mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-mupdf mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-libarchive \
              mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-curl mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gumbo-parser mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-lua
    ./build.sh
The build/ folder then contains ClaudeReader.exe and every DLL it needs.
Single exe without DLLs (what the release ships): build a static OpenCV once, then
    deps/build-opencv.sh
    ./build.sh --static
and take build-static/ClaudeReader.exe.

Linux:
    cmake -S . -B build && cmake --build build && sudo cmake --install build

Command line export (one image per panel), e.g. for a manga:
    ClaudeReader -r -e Comics.cbz ./Exported/ .jpg

Store from the command line:
    ClaudeReader --store list
    ClaudeReader --store mangadex search "yotsuba"
    ClaudeReader --store mangadex chapters <manga id>
    ClaudeReader --store mangadex download <manga id> <chapter id> cbz <library folder>
Writing a store: see README.txt in %APPDATA%\ClaudeReader\sources (created on first use).
